  "fsw_exports": [],
  "description": "Sensor faults on two microsatellites side by side in Sun-safe pointing, with the same sensors. On faulty-sat three have a fault: css-2 is stuck at its largest output, the magnetometer's z axis spikes, and the thermal sensor's reading is stuck at 20 C. healthy-sat shows the true readings.\n\nWhat to look at:\n- css-2 faces away from the Sun: healthy-sat's reads 0, faulty-sat's reads 1.0 all the time.\n- mag-1, z: faulty-sat's reading is now and then three times the field, in about 1 % of the samples; x and y match healthy-sat's.\n- therm-1: healthy-sat's warms from 0 to about 53 C in sunlight and cools in Earth's shadow (from minute 25); faulty-sat's stays at 20 C.\n- Both fly the same attitude: their flight software reads the true state, not these sensors.\n\nTry changing:\n- css-2's fault mode: random (noise instead of the reading).\n- The magnetometer's spike probability, spike amount or fault axis.\n- The thermal sensor's measurement fault mode: spiking.\n\nNote:\n- A fault changes the reading you see. The Sun heading estimated from sun sensors, and the magnetometer of the torque rods' momentum management, use copies of the sensors without faults.",
